In article <ek#@byu.edu>, zimms@gecko.ee.byu.edu (Stephen H. Zimmerman) writes:
>
>I haven't played Nethack in a while and the system I am playing on has version
>3.0i instead of 3.0j.  But I still read this newsgroup--go figure.
>
>So my question is, which of the following spells still exist in the latest version:
>
>	-extra healing
>	-identify
>	-remove curse
>	-finger of death
>	-polymorph
>	-wizard lock
>
>The reason I am wondering is that nobody ever mentions ANY of these spells (albeit some
>of the above are more useful than others) as something to wish for.

I think you wouldn't wish for one because spell books don't really work
all that well in nethack 3.0.  Even if you can read them succesfully, and 
even if you can cast them, you still only get to cast them a few times
before you forget them.

I find for a Priest starting out, simple level 1 spellbooks are better
to have than "finger of death", and other tough ones, because at least
you can learn them and cast them without trouble.  A spell of sleep or
light is kind of nice to have, but a spell of finger of death is 
almost useless because you can't rely on it in a crisis.

I'd say a wand of polymorph/death is a much better wish than the 
corresponding spell.  Similarly, 3 scrolls of identify/remove
curse/extra healing are probably better than 1 spell book.

